<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Spring-Skies.jpg" alt="Plein air painting of the spring skies" width="350" height="482" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Spring Skies. 7x5, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p>Fortune smiled on me today and I managed to do four small studies: two in the studio in preparation for larger paintings, and two done outside in the back yard.</p>
<p>After spending all winter painting in the studio it was a huge treat to be able to lug my gear out into the field behind our house and enjoy a couple of hours standing in the grass.</p>
<p>To get the sky down quickly I applied all the paint with a palette knife, then used large brushes and a palette knife to work the edges. I used the same technique with the tree line and foreground.</p>
<p>Fly included for scale.</p>
